
%9Syntax:%9

BOT%|
BOT %|<botnet>
BOT CLOSE %|<botnet>
BOT CLEANUP%|
BOT HELP%|

%9Parameters:%9

    CLOSE:       Disconnects the botnet without reconnecting: removes
                 pending reconnects, closes the partyline query and the
                 network window. Alias: ZAMKNIJ.
    CLEANUP:     Closes extra connections to the same botnet (the oldest
                 one stays) and removes duplicate reconnects.
    HELP:        Shows this file (via /HELP BOT) or, when it is missing,
                 the help built into the script.

    <botnet>:    A chatnet from the botnet_chatnets list. Case does not
                 matter; a unique prefix of the name is enough.

    Without arguments, prints the state of each botnet: connected (tag,
    minutes since connecting, window number), connecting, reconnecting in
    N s, not responding (reconnecting stopped) or disconnected.

%9Description:%9

    Keeps connections to botnet partylines in order (psotnic, eggdrop and
    similar bots with an IRC interface). A botnet is an ordinary chatnet
    in the erssi configuration; the partyline arrives as a query with the
    nick botnet_partyline_nick. A command of the botnet.pl script.

    /BOT <botnet> runs /CONNECT <botnet>. When the botnet is already
    connected, /CONNECT (also with a server address from the config) does
    not open a second connection but switches to its window; while it is
    still connecting, "is already connecting" is printed. A second
    connection that comes up anyway is closed immediately. A manual
    connect removes pending reconnects.

    Like any network, a botnet has a network window (server messages,
    window name = tag) and, right below it, a single partyline window
    ("partyline:<botnet>"). The query is in place before the bot writes
    anything, so lines from the bot never open new windows; after a
    reconnect they go to the same window. Closing the partyline window
    (/WC, the close button in the web UI) disconnects the botnet without
    reconnecting.

    After a dropped connection at most one reconnect is kept. After
    botnet_reconnect_tries failed attempts in a row reconnecting is
    stopped and a message is printed in the Notices window; /BOT <botnet>
    resumes it. When loaded, the script tidies up just like CLEANUP.

%9Statusbar:%9

    The "botnet" item shows each botnet: ● connected, ◌ connecting,
    ↻ reconnecting in N s, ✕ reconnecting stopped, ○ disconnected. Next
    to a connected botnet, the number of partyline lines you have not
    seen yet - in red when someone mentioned your nick; it disappears
    when you enter the window. To add it (the window bar is "info" in
    erssi, "window" in many configurations):

        /STATUSBAR info ADD -after act botnet

    The look is set with /FORMAT botnet_sb_up, _unread, _hilight,
    _connecting, _retry, _stopped, _down and _label.

%9Settings:%9

    botnet_chatnets = (built-in list)
        Chatnets treated as botnets, separated by spaces or commas.
    botnet_partyline_nick = partyline
        The nick the hub uses for the partyline.
    botnet_reconnect_tries = 3
        Failed reconnects in a row before giving up; 0 = no limit.
    botnet_quit_message =
        Quit message when disconnecting; empty = erssi's default.
    botnet_statusbar_all = ON
        Also show disconnected botnets in the statusbar.
    botnet_statusbar_list =
        Botnets shown in the statusbar, separated by spaces; empty = all
        of botnet_chatnets. The others still work as botnets, they are
        only left out of the statusbar.

%9Examples:%9

    /BOT
    /BOT hub
    /BOT CLOSE hub
    /BOT CLEANUP

